From: brainux-pw-a9300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: imx28-pwa7200: give the bookmark, home and dictionary menu keys a code

The keyboard MCU sends 0x25 (Bookmark), 0x24 (Home) and 0x2b (Dictionary
Menu), but the keymap leaves them out, so the driver drops them. Map them
to F13, F14 and F15 in both the normal and the symbol keymap. These have
no fixed meaning in X (XF86Tools, XF86Launch5, XF86Launch6), so what they
do can be chosen in userspace.

Checked on PW-A9300: the three keys arrive as F13, F14 and F15.

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx28-pwa7200.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx28-pwa7200.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx28-pwa7200.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx28-pwa7200.dts
@@ -69,9 +69,9 @@
 		<0x15 KEY_PAGEDOWN>,  /* Kogo */
 		<0x1c KEY_INSERT>,    /* Britannica */
 		<0x1d KEY_DELETE>,    /* Switch */
-		/* <0x25 >, */        /* Bookmark */
-		/* <0x24 >, */        /* Home */
-		/* <0x2b >, */        /* Dictionary Menu */
+		<0x25 KEY_F13>,       /* Bookmark */
+		<0x24 KEY_F14>,       /* Home */
+		<0x2b KEY_F15>,       /* Dictionary Menu */
 		<0x02 KEY_Q>,         /* Q */
 		<0x08 KEY_W>,         /* W */
 		<0x0e KEY_E>,         /* E */
@@ -119,9 +119,9 @@
 		<0x15 KEY_PAGEDOWN>,  /* Kogo */
 		<0x1c KEY_INSERT>,    /* Britannica */
 		<0x1d KEY_DELETE>,    /* Switch */
-		/* <0x25 >, */        /* Bookmark */
-		/* <0x24 >, */        /* Home */
-		/* <0x2b >, */        /* Dictionary Menu */
+		<0x25 KEY_F13>,       /* Bookmark */
+		<0x24 KEY_F14>,       /* Home */
+		<0x2b KEY_F15>,       /* Dictionary Menu */
 		<0x02 KEY_1>,          /* Q */
 		<0x08 KEY_2>,          /* W */
 		<0x0e KEY_3>,          /* E */
